---
description: Research2Paper repository workflow for maintaining the paper-writing skill, prompt templates, draft checker and privacy boundaries.
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use `skills/research2paper/SKILL.md` as the canonical workflow for paper drafting, revision, reviewer-response and pre-submission tasks.
- Keep long writing rules in `skills/research2paper/references/`; do not duplicate full templates in IDE rule files.
- Preserve fidelity to the supplied research material. Do not invent data, statistics, citations, novelty or completed experiments; use `[MISSING: ...]` markers.
- Do not commit unpublished papers, raw data, generated drafts, personal data, API keys, tokens, local usernames or local absolute paths.
- When editing skill files, keep `.claude/skills/research2paper` identical to `skills/research2paper` and run `python -m unittest discover -s tests`.
